2. Definitions

"Paid Software" is software for which an external user must pay to obtain,
access, use or unlock the software or any of its features. This includes
one-time purchases, subscriptions, license fees, paid tiers, paid feature
unlocks and paid access to hosted software. Integration of the Covered Material
into Paid Software is covered even if the capture feature itself is free.
A mandatory payment through a distributor or another intermediary also counts.

"Free Software" in this license means software provided to its users without
any software access, usage or feature fee. It describes price, not an assertion
that the software satisfies an open-source or free-software definition.
Advertising revenue, voluntary sponsorship and optional donations do not make
software Paid Software, provided payment is not required for software access,
use or features. This permission applies to software published by individuals,
companies and other organizations alike.

"Internal Use" means use within an organization for its own operations,
including its business operations and internal development, without providing
the Covered Material as part of Paid Software to external users.

